    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34578" root="فلك" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْلَكُونٌ</span></b>  The <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُوبَق</span> [or <i>baker's rolling-pin:</i> see
the latter word]: (O, K, TA: [in the CK, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">السَّوِيقُ</span>
is erroneously put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الشُّوبَقُ</span>:]) Az holds both of
these words to be arabicized. (O.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And (TA)
The <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرْدِىّ</span> [or <i>papyrus</i>]. (S; and K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فلكن</span>.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <i>Tar,</i> or <i>pitch;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَارٌ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفْتٌ</span>. (K. n
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فلكن</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَوْسٌ فَيْلَكُونٌ</span> <i>A great bow.</i>
(TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فلكن</span>.)

